1. **An image display system comprising:**

a display device configured to display a first graphical object having a first value of an attribute parameter;

an input sensor configured to receive user input relative to the display device;

a memory storing instructions; and

one or more processors operatively coupled to the display device, the input sensor, and the memory, the one or more processors configured, upon execution of the instructions, to:

detect, based on the user input, a directional swipe applied to the first graphical object;

identify a second graphical object associated with the first graphical object based at least in part on a direction of the directional swipe, the second graphical object having a second value of the attribute parameter different from the first value; and

replace, on the display device, the first graphical object with the second graphical object.

1. A display system comprising:  

   acquisition means for acquiring information indicating an input position on a display screen;  

   extraction means for extracting, based on the acquired information, a first display object corresponding to the input position and a second display object related to the first display object;  

   storage means for storing relationship information associating the first display object with the second display object; and  

   display control means for controlling display of the first display object and, in response to determining that the input position has moved in a first direction beyond a predetermined threshold, causing the second display object related to the first display object to be displayed on the display screen.

1. A computer-implemented method comprising:

displaying, by a computing device, a first object on a display;

detecting a user gesture that moves the first object across the display;

determining that a component of the movement in a predetermined direction exceeds a threshold distance;

in response to the determining, retrieving a second object associated with the first object, the second object having a value of an attribute corresponding to the predetermined direction that differs from a value of the attribute of the first object; and

causing the second object to be displayed in place of the first object.

1. An image browsing apparatus comprising:

display means for displaying a current image;

storage means for storing a plurality of images and attributes relating the plurality of images;

touch-operation acquisition means for acquiring a direction and a distance of a touch operation performed while the current image is displayed;

selection means for selecting, from the storage means, a related image using an attribute associated with the acquired direction and based on the acquired distance; and

replacement means for replacing the current image displayed by the display means with the selected related image.
